From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:54:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ship the statically-embedded subprojects' licences in wheel
 metadata

glslang, Vulkan-Headers, libp2p and zimg are meson-wrap subprojects
fetched and compiled in at build time (glslang "embedded statically
and always present" per meson.build; libp2p/zimg linked into the core
unconditionally); none of their licences are in this checkout or in
the wheel. license-files is an explicit list here, so there is no
default glob to extend it with - widen the list directly to add
LICENSE.glslang, LICENSE.vulkan-headers, COPYING.libp2p and
COPYING.zimg, staged at the project root by the workflow from each
subproject's own release tag (pinned for glslang/Vulkan-Headers;
libp2p/zimg's wraps pin revision = HEAD, so their notice is fetched
from the default branch, same lack of pinning as upstream's own build).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 46700e2..6049406 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ description = "A frameserver for the 21st century"
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.12"
 license = "LGPL-2.1-or-later"
-license-files = ["COPYING.LESSER"]
+license-files = ["COPYING.LESSER", "LICENSE.glslang", "LICENSE.vulkan-headers", "COPYING.libp2p", "COPYING.zimg"]
 authors = [{ name = "Fredrik Mellbin", email = "fredrik.mellbin@gmail.com" }]
 keywords = ["frameserver", "video", "audio"]
 classifiers = [
